        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f641f84c-bc27-56a1-bf47-ee51ee237382",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Marcus Welby, M.D.\n- People: Robert Young, James Brolin, Elena Verdugo, Randolph Mantooth, Josh Brolin, Barbra Streisand\n- Roles: Marcus Welby, Steve Kiley, Consuelo Lopez\n- Companies: ABC, Universal\n- Places: California\n\nFacts:\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. was an American medical drama television program that aired on ABC on Tuesdays from 10:00 to 11:00 p.m. EST from September 23, 1969 to July 29, 1976.\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. starred Robert Young as Marcus Welby, a family practitioner known for a kind bedside manner, close relationships with patients, and making house calls.\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. starred James Brolin as Steve Kiley, a younger doctor and Welby’s partner.\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. starred Elena Verdugo as Consuelo Lopez, the nurse and office manager for Welby and Kiley.\n- After signing with Universal and moving to California, Randolph Mantooth gradually built his résumé with appearances on Adam-12, Marcus Welby, M.D., McCloud, and Alias Smith and Jones between 1968 and 1971.\n- James Brolin, born Craig Kenneth Bruderlin on July 18, 1940, is an American actor, producer, and director known for film and television roles, including sitcoms and soap operas.\n- James Brolin is the father of actor Josh Brolin and the husband of singer and actress Barbra Streisand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3dc72f79-0cc2-5b7f-82be-29dabd908cba",
        "text": "Page: Marcus Welby, M.D.. Sentence: Marcus Welby, M.D. was an American medical drama television program that aired Tuesdays at 10:00–11:00 p.m. (EST) on ABC from September 23, 1969 to July 29, 1976.\nPage: Marcus Welby, M.D.. Sentence: It starred Robert Young as the title character, a family practitioner with a kind bedside manner, who was on a first name basis with many of his patients (and who also made house-calls), James Brolin, as Steve Kiley, M.D, a younger doctor who played Welby's partner, and Elena Verdugo, who played Welby and Kiley's dedicated and loving nurse and office manager, Consuelo Lopez.\nPage: James Brolin. Sentence: James Brolin ( ; born Craig Kenneth Bruderlin, July 18, 1940) is an American actor, producer, and director, best known for his roles in film and television, including sitcoms and soap operas.\nPage: James Brolin. Sentence: He is the father of actor Josh Brolin and husband of singer/actress Barbra Streisand.\nPage: Randolph Mantooth. Sentence: After signing with Universal and moving to California, he slowly built up his resume with work on such dramatic series as \"Adam-12\" (1968), \"Marcus Welby, M.D.\" (1969), \"McCloud\" (1970) and \"Alias Smith and Jones\" (1971).",
